# base.packages and aur.packages names the CachyOS layer (cachyos.packages)
# replaces. A CachyOS install never carries them: pacstrap and the AUR step leave
# them out, the offline ISO does not bake them, and the installer records them in
# the provisioning ledger so `ryoku update` does not deliver them later. One
# package per line.

# The stock kernel: CachyOS boots linux-cachyos with linux-cachyos-lts as the
# fallback. linux-headers is not listed: ryoku-desktop depends on it by name
# (for xpadneo-dkms) and no CachyOS headers package provides that name, so it
# lands with the desktop either way.
linux

# The AUR helper: CachyOS ships yay in [cachyos], so the box updates it from the
# repo instead of carrying an AUR build of yay-bin.
yay-bin
